course: dictionary
lesson: 8905
title: Shut: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shut is a small word with a big job. Most of the time it means closed, like a door, a window, a box or your eyes. «The door shut behind her with a click.» The door closed, so shut means closed.
explain: Shut can also describe something that is closed. «The shop was shut on Sunday» tells you the shop was not open. The words around shut give you the clue.
explain: When a shop or place shuts, it stops being open for business. «The pool shuts at eight o'clock» means you cannot swim there after eight. Opening and closing times are clues, just like the clues in a story.
fact: Shut means closed, like a door, a window, a box or your eyes.
fact: Shut can be a verb: you shut the gate, he shuts the fridge, they shut the window.
fact: The word stays the same in the past: «She shut the gate yesterday.»
fact: When a shop or place shuts, it stops being open for business.
fact: «Shut down» can mean turn off a computer or close a business. «Shut up» means stop talking, but it is rude, so say «Please be quiet» instead.
exercise: «The potoo sits still on a branch and, even with its eyes shut, it can still see.» What does shut mean here? | Full of water | *Closed | Hidden under a leaf | Opened wide
exercise: «The shop shuts at six o'clock.» What does shuts mean? | *Stops being open for business | Moves to the top shelf | Gets bigger and bigger | Starts singing loudly
exercise: «A girl climbed into the dryer, and the door shut behind her.» Find and copy one word that means closed. | dryer | girl | climbed | *shut
test: Every morning, Sam ___ the gate so the dog stays safe. Which word fits? | shutted | shutting | *shuts | shutter
test: «Shut up» is rude. What should you say instead? | Sing a song | Close the bus | Shut down the room | *Please be quiet
exam: Which sentence uses shut to mean closed? | «The shop shuts at six.» | «Shut up, the film is starting.» | *«Please shut the fridge door.»
